= R13 pair-table prefetch gate: replacement-host run

*Status, 2026-10-27:* Five-round A/A and paired suite completed on EC2 instance `i-048baef2256adcc25`. The frozen holdout remains incomplete after two 60-attempt isolation stops on its final missing candidate row. The runner retained 267 holdout price records. This report records an incomplete run; it does not promote a Table A row.

The pre-timing protocol is `research/ic_tool_program/rounds/R13-prefetch-gate/PROTOCOL.md`. The candidate uses the admitted-run prefetch pass only for stored pair tables with at least 1,000,000 entries. Source revisions were base `261482646ee89b332dca69e2f296b0774c25d2c2` and candidate `efc6336d55c59cceb92cb82de73598ebe15ff3ca`. Both binaries were built on the run host with rustc 1.99.1 and the same Cargo.lock. The host was an Intel Xeon 6975P-C `m8i.8xlarge` in us-east-2b; isolation reserved both SMT siblings, CPUs 2 and 18, with one Rayon thread and unset `KIC_RHO_CANON`. The host manifest, runner configuration, raw records and refusal log are in the separate `runs-host-048baef2/` tree, copied to the R13 checkpoint store.

Before timing, native host-class checks passed, 24 frozen holdouts regenerated byte-for-byte, and 90/90 historical pin outputs matched. The A/A control completed 220 scheduled records and eight retained retry records with no missing cold pairs. At K0/F2^57, its base/copy cold ratio was 0.984873 with native 95% interval [0.976267, 0.993554]. The paired suite completed 400 scheduled records and 25 retries, again with no missing cold pairs.

